{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres","id":1523420,"title":"Using the spheres","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-01T08:40:07-07:00","id":1523420,"title":"Using the spheres","content":"It's is possibly use the sphere Mind to cause reactions in the body awhile is biology still need Life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T12:06:47-07:00","id":1523430,"title":"","content":"The book do address this:<br /> <br /> Basically, yes. If you scare someone with Mind, their body will respond to fear as it would to natural fear. If you use Life to increase someone's cortisol levels they'll have a negative mood response.<br /> <br /> The line is that this is indirect and individuals don't react to stimuli in the same fashion. If you're just using Mind, you don't know what someone's baseline hormone levels are and other factors, so you don't have solid control over what the biological response will be. One person might pass out from fear, and another respond by becoming biologically activated and ready to physically respond to danger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T00:01:26-07:00","id":1523456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523430#post1523430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book do address this:<br /> <br /> Basically, yes. If you scare someone with Mind, their body will respond to fear as it would to natural fear. If you use Life to increase someone's cortisol levels they'll have a negative mood response.<br /> <br /> The line is that this is indirect and individuals don't react to stimuli in the same fashion. If you're just using Mind, you don't know what someone's baseline hormone levels are and other factors, so you don't have solid control over what the biological response will be. One person might pass out from fear, and another respond by becoming biologically activated and ready to physically respond to danger.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, like many things about da book, is one of the many things I never liked.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hormone&quot; levels is a bloody technocratic thing. It shouldn't universally apply. Specially not for a hermetic operating under the &quot;4 bodily humors&quot; or some such.<br /> <br /> I swear, the writers often forget about thinking in the game within the game's terms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T01:39:25-07:00","id":1523457,"title":"","content":"Ultimately the grip doesn't change the basics of how the separation of Life and Mind interact when used on a living creature. Directly manipulating &quot;humors&quot; is Life, but can have emotional consequence. How you describe it doesn't really change the way things work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T02:11:56-07:00","id":1523458,"title":"","content":"<br /> Generally speaking a lot of it will depend on your mage\u2019s understanding of the nature of Mind Body Duality. If your mage considers the mind to be an entirely seperate thing from the body, then no, Mind effects will not be able to affect how the body works.<br /> <br /> If instead you see them as linked inherently, then there is room for some influence, but without Life, that influence will be like hitting a billiard ball with a cue. You can set it up, but it will be outside your immediate control once you let the ball go, whereas having Life in addition would let you control all the balls in the table.<br /> <br /> some example paradigms:<br /> <br /> Humourism, an hippocratic idea where the body is composed of four humours which have an influence on the welfare of the body and the mind. Such mages would probably see affecting the mind via the humours as having knock on effects on health, but without Life they would be unable to control said outcome beyond a being more melancholic making the body less capable of fighting disease, or sanguine making the body more probe to fight or flight response, for example.<br /> <br /> Platonic dualism states that the mind is trapped within the body, and that everything perceived is filtered by the body, abstracting it away from truth. Mind magic would therefor be a way to move beyond these limitations and experience that which the body conceals, not enhancing senses so much as bypassing them. Such mages would be unable to affect the body via Mind magic, but could definitely affect the Mind via Life<br /> <br /> Mind body indivisability states that the two are seperate but inherently linked entities, and that some, such as Descartes, proclaim these is a physical link between the two, such as the pineal gland, but others may instead argue that they are tied together via the soul, one\u2019s chakras, or even their past lives. Such mages would see mind affecting body as easily as Life affecting mind, so long as their magic stimulates aspects of what it is they believe connects it, such as stimulating the pineal gland, or rerouting energy through the soul (would not require spirit unless you wanted to change the nature of their soul at the same time) humourism can be considered to fit here, though I included it separately since someone specifically cited it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Property dualism is the idea that the mind cannot be constrained to physical phenomena, that the mind exists outside of the physical, possible within the astral umbra or within its own unique realm deep in the dreaming, for such mages Life magic would have very limited impact on the mind, but Mind magic may indeed still affect the body as while the mind is outside of the body, it also heavily influences the material bound mind. The mind can supervene upon the body. But perhaps only when it comes to perceptions, such as Mental sensation of pain translating to physically felt pain, or mental sensations of cold becoming actual hypothermia<br /> <br /> this is not a complete list nor is it a comprehensive account. But the idea is the possibility of Mind and Life spheres influencing each other\u2019s purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T05:47:45-07:00","id":1523543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523456#post1523456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Hormone&quot; levels is a bloody technocratic thing. It shouldn't universally apply. Specially not for a hermetic operating under the &quot;4 bodily humors&quot; or some such.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may not be an entirely bad thing. Hormone levels is (mostly) a technocratic thing, but the technocrats have been winning the Ascension War for centuries. By default, on Earth, the consensus reality is a baseline that has largely been set by the Technocracy. There\u2019s undoubtedly a lot more that the Technocrats would like to make part of consensus reality - super-science that is still well in advance of the consensus, and always will be because the technocracy keeps advancing as well - but endocrinology (even in it\u2019s modern form) is not a new field any more.<br /> <br /> Of course, mystic mages don\u2019t work (entirely) within consensus reality. Depending on paradigm, it may be reasonable for a mystic to use mind-affecting magic to affect a target\u2019s body, or body-affecting magic to affect their mind, in ways that go beyond leveraging the consensus reality. But you know what we call it when a mage induces an effect that goes outside of consensus reality? Magick.<br /> <br /> And in game terms, a mage who has the ability to affect a living body in ways that are beyond consensus reality is using Life sphere Magick. A mage who has the ability to affect a person\u2019s mind in ways that are beyond consensus reality is using Mind sphere Magick. This is so even if the mage\u2019s paradigm says it isn\u2019t; even if the mage\u2019s paradigm doesn\u2019t include the spheres at all.<br /> <br /> But that is just game mechanics. We need not read too much into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11151,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","user":"travisjhall","date":". 10-04-2023, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T14:27:16-07:00","id":1523737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523543#post1523543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That may not be an entirely bad thing. Hormone levels is (mostly) a technocratic thing, but the technocrats have been winning the Ascension War for centuries. By default, on Earth, the consensus reality is a baseline that has largely been set by the Technocracy. There\u2019s undoubtedly a lot more that the Technocrats would like to make part of consensus reality - super-science that is still well in advance of the consensus, and always will be because the technocracy keeps advancing as well - but endocrinology (even in it\u2019s modern form) is not a new field any more.<br /> <br /> Of course, mystic mages don\u2019t work (entirely) within consensus reality. Depending on paradigm, it may be reasonable for a mystic to use mind-affecting magic to affect a target\u2019s body, or body-affecting magic to affect their mind, in ways that go beyond leveraging the consensus reality. But you know what we call it when a mage induces an effect that goes outside of consensus reality? Magick.<br /> <br /> And in game terms, a mage who has the ability to affect a living body in ways that are beyond consensus reality is using Life sphere Magick. A mage who has the ability to affect a person\u2019s mind in ways that are beyond consensus reality is using Mind sphere Magick. This is so even if the mage\u2019s paradigm says it isn\u2019t; even if the mage\u2019s paradigm doesn\u2019t include the spheres at all.<br /> <br /> But that is just game mechanics. We need not read too much into it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consensus is as real in the game as any bogus pseudoscientific nonsense that you could imagine. The truth is that MtA (WoD in general actually) is basically Gnosticism. The best description possible for it would be the Immateriallism of Emmanuel Kant.<br /> <br /> I could just as easily make the claim that, the GAME MECHANIC that we know as &quot;Spheres&quot; should NOT have Mind affecting the body, nor have Life affecting emotions or whatever.<br /> <br /> Then, when you say that your Techie has the paradigm that he can control emotional states by manipulating hormones (and whatever else other technobabble), this doesn't change the game mechanics - he still use the game Mechanics of Mind 2 and just simply believes to be &quot;changing hormones' levels&quot; instead of using some &quot;hipnotic waves&quot; or whatever.<br /> <br /> Still, that's the core of the problem in its entirety, the Spheres and their effects are awfully badly written. And one of the reason is this, searching for scientific explanations when in the game they are just as valid as an &quot;evil eye&quot; for an explanation.<br /> <br /> There's no more reason to allow that than there is to not allow it. In my opinion however, it just creates unnecessary overlap and confusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T16:20:58-07:00","id":1523743,"title":"","content":"By that logic magic shouldn't be able to cause damage to living things without Life. &quot;Shooting someone with a hypertech pistol,&quot; and, &quot;casting a fireball,&quot; are just how paradigms explain Life 3 damage effects.<br /> <br /> Life impacts mental well-being, and Mind impacts physical well-being, the same way Forces does: indirectly through natural processes. Forces can adjust ambient temperatures, and keep you from freezing to death or dying from heat stroke... or Forces and electrocute you to death because death is what happen if you hit a human body with enough electricity.<br /> <br /> That's all the books are saying about Life and Mind: if you mess with someone using one, the normal consequences happen; just like the normal consequences of being exposed to fire summoned with Forces happens.<br /> <br /> You're vastly over complicating what's a very simple concept. If you use magic to change something, normal consequences will resume (as per Consensus/local Reality Zone) once the magic is resolved. In normal play, you're operating under the Consensus, and that means the natural consequences include the fact that there isn't a hard separation of mind and body even if there is one in the Spheres. If you use Mind to cause mental stress, the body will respond naturally to increased stress triggers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T17:00:02-07:00","id":1523744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523737#post1523737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consensus is as real in the game as any bogus pseudoscientific nonsense that you could imagine. The truth is that MtA (WoD in general actually) is basically Gnosticism. The best description possible for it would be the Immateriallism of Emmanuel Kant.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be true - arguably - for a perfectly enlightened soul (with Arete 10), but we aren\u2019t usually playing characters with Arete 10. Mages might aspire to Gnosticism or Immaterialism, but the fact is that they operate for the most part within consensus reality.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s consensus reality that allows everybody, including Mages, to do things without having to roll Arete, and without accumulating paradox on a botch. It\u2019s only once mages start violating the consensus that they have to roll Arete, and worry about coincidence, vulgarity, and paradox.<br /> <br /> And if I Magickally create a sword, I only have to worry about the vulgarity and paradox of the creation. I can attack with that sword, and doing so remains within the consensus, and I don\u2019t accumulate paradox with each attack (even on a botch). Likewise, if a mage uses Life sphere Magick to conjure hormones, that initial conjuration is magickal, subject to vulgarity, paradox, the limits of my Arete, but once summoned those hormones can affect someone\u2019s emotions just like any other (non-magickal) hormones.<br /> <br /> However, we also have to bear in mind that working this way is subject to the constraints of the consensus. Hormones are not a terribly reliable way to spur a target into a particular action, in consensus reality. If you want a super-specific result from applying hormones - something like what Poison Ivy does in Batman comics - you\u2019re probably going to need to go beyond consensus reality, and for that you need Mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523737#post1523737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could just as easily make the claim that, the GAME MECHANIC that we know as &quot;Spheres&quot; should NOT have Mind affecting the body, nor have Life affecting emotions or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is what I said. If you use the Mind sphere to produce a Magick effect, you can\u2019t directly affect the body with that effect. And Life cannot directly affect emotions.<br /> <br /> But once conjured with Forces, fire burns without paradox, because that\u2019s consensus reality. Once conjured with Matter, lead is heavy, because that\u2019s consensus reality. And once conjured adrenaline courses through a person\u2019s body, as the effect of Life Magick, they\u2019re probably going to feel pretty jumpy, because in consensus reality that\u2019s something that adrenaline does.<br /> <br /> I think sometimes some of us forget that Mage: the Ascension is a game about a conflict over what reality is. That conflict makes no sense if the consensus reality does nothing, and the rules definitely tell us that consensus reality matters. Maybe some of us like the idea of playing in a setting where there isn\u2019t a default baseline reality, but that\u2019s not what this setting gives us by default.<br /> <br /> (And then, of course, there\u2019s reality zones as well - places where the consensus isn\u2019t what it usually is.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T04:16:52-07:00","id":1523766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>travisjhall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523744#post1523744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might be true - arguably - for a perfectly enlightened soul (with Arete 10), but we aren\u2019t usually playing characters with Arete 10. Mages might aspire to Gnosticism or Immaterialism, but the fact is that they operate for the most part within consensus reality.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s consensus reality that allows everybody, including Mages, to do things without having to roll Arete, and without accumulating paradox on a botch. It\u2019s only once mages start violating the consensus that they have to roll Arete, and worry about coincidence, vulgarity, and paradox.<br /> <br /> And if I Magickally create a sword, I only have to worry about the vulgarity and paradox of the creation. I can attack with that sword, and doing so remains within the consensus, and I don\u2019t accumulate paradox with each attack (even on a botch). Likewise, if a mage uses Life sphere Magick to conjure hormones, that initial conjuration is magickal, subject to vulgarity, paradox, the limits of my Arete, but once summoned those hormones can affect someone\u2019s emotions just like any other (non-magickal) hormones.<br /> <br /> However, we also have to bear in mind that working this way is subject to the constraints of the consensus. Hormones are not a terribly reliable way to spur a target into a particular action, in consensus reality. If you want a super-specific result from applying hormones - something like what Poison Ivy does in Batman comics - you\u2019re probably going to need to go beyond consensus reality, and for that you need Mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Which is what I said. If you use the Mind sphere to produce a Magick effect, you can\u2019t directly affect the body with that effect. And Life cannot directly affect emotions.<br /> <br /> But once conjured with Forces, fire burns without paradox, because that\u2019s consensus reality. Once conjured with Matter, lead is heavy, because that\u2019s consensus reality. And once conjured adrenaline courses through a person\u2019s body, as the effect of Life Magick, they\u2019re probably going to feel pretty jumpy, because in consensus reality that\u2019s something that adrenaline does.<br /> <br /> I think sometimes some of us forget that Mage: the Ascension is a game about a conflict over what reality is. That conflict makes no sense if the consensus reality does nothing, and the rules definitely tell us that consensus reality matters. Maybe some of us like the idea of playing in a setting where there isn\u2019t a default baseline reality, but that\u2019s not what this setting gives us by default.<br /> <br /> (And then, of course, there\u2019s reality zones as well - places where the consensus isn\u2019t what it usually is.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, it makes sense.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... Interesting. So, we could say that the &quot;magik&quot; of the Traditions truly only reinforce the Technocratic Consensus, rather than trying to deny it. Perhaps the Taftani are right on that one after all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T06:40:43-07:00","id":1523771,"title":"","content":"Okay, this got out of hand a little. Anyway, here's another question. Supposing that a Technomage, whether traditional or a technocrat, wanted to download information from a person's memory and transfer it to a machine, like a smartphone for example, what spheres would be needed? I believe that as there is transference, so Correspondence 2 is necessary and Mind 2 (at least) since it involves memories, but would anything else be necessary? Life or Matter, perhaps.<br /> <br /> Also, let's avoid going into the subject of how much human memory fits in a machine's memory, that's not the focus.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T12:24:10-07:00","id":1523780,"title":"","content":"It's a Mind (2-4)/Forces 3 effect. The level of Mind depends on what kind of information you're looking for, and Mind+Forces would allow you to convert thoughts into digital information. Correspondence isn't necessary as long as the target is within normal sensory range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T15:12:17-07:00","id":1523786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523780#post1523780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a Mind (2-4)/Forces 3 effect. The level of Mind depends on what kind of information you're looking for, and Mind+Forces would allow you to convert thoughts into digital information. Correspondence isn't necessary as long as the target is within normal sensory range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why Forces?<br /> <br /> This is a problem I have with this game, and I think that players have, but it is also a problem that the writters themselves have (and which end up confusing the players and thus infects the players with the same problem) of just selecting a random collection of Spheres for effects based on the &quot;feeling&quot;.<br /> <br /> Like for example, &quot;Chi healing&quot; requiring Prime because of the &quot;feeling&quot; about &quot;Chi&quot;.<br /> <br /> No, to determine what Spheres are necessary we need strict adherence to what each level of a Sphere does.<br /> <br /> What does Forces 3 do? It turns one form of energy into another. For example, heat turned into light, or &quot;cold&quot; turned into &quot;shadow&quot; (scientific paradigms may see &quot;cold&quot; and &quot;shadow&quot; as mere absence of heat and light respectively, but mystical paradigms may see those are active and just opposed forces). <br /> <br /> If you combine with other Spheres, you could turn a non forces pattern into a forces pattern or vice versa. For example, Matter 2 Forces 3 to turn a lightning into silver (or if you want a more coincidental effect, to make glass if the lighting is in an area with sand). Or, you could turn an apple into an explosive device with Life 2 Forces 3 (transmuting the apple into heat+kinetic force).<br /> <br /> With that knowledge, I ask you: are you turning thoughts into electricity or something like it?<br /> <br /> Well, you may say that you are, but the problem is that, once you do it, those thoughts are GONE.<br /> <br /> Mind 2-4 + Forces 3 would just be something Matrix-like, turning human brains into living batteries. And that's it. You do NOT store those thoughts.<br /> <br /> Imo you would need to use Mind 2-4 to &quot;extract&quot; the thoughts obviously (Mind 1 even, for superficial thoughts and impressions, Mind 2 for emotional states of the target, Mind 3 to capture dreams and whatever the target might be thinking at the time of the effect, but if you want to extract all of the most hidden and deep thoughts of the target, Mind 4).<br /> <br /> Then, to imprint those mental patterns into an object (be it a pen drive or the vase of the ancestors memory) you need Prime between 2 to 4 (up to Prime 5 if it is to imprint onto a living being - in a manner different from giving the living being those memories - aka the living being becomes a vessel for those mental patterns, but not a user).<br /> <br /> Prime is needed to change a pattern and to allow imprinting something into a pattern.<br /> <br /> Forces just simply doesn't do anything like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T21:31:44-07:00","id":1523805,"title":"","content":"The good thing about the sphere system is that you can do a lot of things with creativity, the bad part, however, is this confusion with what does what.<br /> <br /> And here's a question: Aren't thoughts already electrical impulses?\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T00:08:01-07:00","id":1523809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523766#post1523766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm... Interesting. So, we could say that the &quot;magik&quot; of the Traditions truly only reinforce the Technocratic Consensus, rather than trying to deny it. Perhaps the Taftani are right on that one after all</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. Sorcery is supported by the consensus reality as well. Do you think that comes from the Technocrats?<br /> <br /> No. The Technocracy has influenced the consensus, but it is not entirely within their control. It\u2019s not the Technocratic Consensus; it\u2019s human Consensus.<br /> <br /> As for fully denying it, there\u2019s an argument to be made that doing so would be Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T01:30:57-07:00","id":1523810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523786#post1523786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why Forces?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Forces governs base digital information, and that's what we're turning Mind Patterns into. If you want to turn a person into a stone statue, you need Life and Matter. If you want to turn thoughts/memories - which are Mind Patterns - into digital information - which is a type of Forces Pattern - you use both Spheres. This is very well established in the rules. <br /> <br /> It also an example in the books, that if you want to display your surface thoughts as a projection of light, it's a Forces 3/Mind 2 effect. This is just to take it from &quot;holographic display&quot; to &quot;store-able digital information.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a problem I have with this game,... </div> </div> </div>You can always just go away if you don't have more to do in this thread but complain about the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like for example, &quot;Chi healing&quot; requiring Prime because of the &quot;feeling&quot; about &quot;Chi&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Yes, a lot of us think HDYDT utterly failed at it's job. You're not saying anything useful with this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, to determine what Spheres are necessary we need strict adherence to what each level of a Sphere does. </div> </div> </div>Besides the fact that I did, it's impossible to do what you're asking, because of two important factors. First, the Spheres are inherently abstract and have levels of interpretation. There are always going to be effects that one person feels should be an X level one, that someone else feels is going to be a Y level effect. Even the far better delineated version of the system in Awakening 2e only lessens the impact of this, it can't remove it completely. Second for most intentions there are multiple potential effects that could accomplish the task. Life 3 is the most obvious way to heal someone, but you can create a Wonder with a Life 2 effect they activate (or it activates on its own), high level Entropy can repair instead of destroy, Matter can create medicines and so on, Spirit can call on spirits with healing powers, etc.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What does Forces 3 do? </div> </div> </div>The book literally says Forces 3 combined with Mind allows you to convert thoughts into energy. Don't lecture about strict adherence to what the Spheres do what Forces 3 explicitly does this when combined with other Spheres according to its description. .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With that knowledge, I ask you: are you turning thoughts into electricity or something like it? </div> </div> </div>Electrical information is expressed as electrical patterns, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, you may say that you are, but the problem is that, once you do it, those thoughts are GONE. </div> </div> </div>Or you just copy them since that's within the Sphere levels being used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You do NOT store those thoughts. </div> </div> </div>Why can't you store them?<br /> <br /> If I change water into air, I can breathe the air. I could put the air in a balloon and float the balloon. It doesn't cease to exist as it's new form.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then, to imprint those mental patterns into an object (be it a pen drive or the vase of the ancestors memory) you need Prime between 2 to 4 (up to Prime 5 if it is to imprint onto a living being - in a manner different from giving the living being those memories - aka the living being becomes a vessel for those mental patterns, but not a user). </div> </div> </div>Do I need Prime to put air turned into water into a glass?<br /> <br /> Digital information isn't magic. You don't need to &quot;imprint it.&quot; You simply capture the information with Forces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prime is needed to change a pattern and to allow imprinting something into a pattern. </div> </div> </div>Neither of these is true the way you're stating them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Forces just simply doesn't do anything like it. </div> </div> </div>Life 5/Forces 3 lets you copy the Human Torch's living fire and flight powers. You don't need any Prime for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T05:20:00-07:00","id":1523814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523805#post1523805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here's a question: Aren't thoughts already electrical impulses?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Under a strict Technocratic paradigm. I'm not sure that even the Etherites or VAs would agree on that thou, to say nothing about any other paradigms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T06:14:43-07:00","id":1523815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523810#post1523810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because Forces governs base digital information, and that's what we're turning Mind Patterns into. If you want to turn a person into a stone statue, you need Life and Matter. If you want to turn thoughts/memories - which are Mind Patterns - into digital information - which is a type of Forces Pattern - you use both Spheres. This is very well established in the rules.</div> </div> </div> </div> And this would be just another one of the many examples upon which your sacred &quot;rules&quot; are just utterly dumb or broken. Ramnses did a post not too long ago that displayed the many inconsistencies of the holy rules that you are so fervently advocating for, with some absolutely nonsensical combinations printed on official books, born out exactly from that problem that different writters apparently don't fully understand the system and just goes with the &quot;feeling&quot; of it. If you want to, I could name DOZENS of examples of nonsensical &quot;rules&quot;, which just create confusion and misunderstanding amongst the player base, which is why we have an endless amount of posts on forums asking how to use the Sphere, a problem that wouldn't occur if the rules had been written on solid foundations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also an example in the books, that if you want to display your surface thoughts as a projection of light, it's a Forces 3/Mind 2 effect. This is just to take it from &quot;holographic display&quot; to &quot;store-able digital information.&quot; </div> </div> </div> Again, here we have another stupid effect. You can already use Forces to create holograms; and believe it or not, Magik is already commanded by your thoughts. The only way this could ever be useful is if you want to make this effect permanent (in order to dismiss the -1 from cumulative effects) and that it can change by itself without need for concentration, or if you want to display the thoughts of another being.<br /> <br /> Besides all that, my question is: so what? What does that have to do with what I'm saying?<br /> <br /> Oh, I can also use Mind 2 Entropy 1 to make a dice always roll a number I want without me having to concentrate on it. And what does that have to do with anything?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can always just go away if you don't have more to do in this thread but complain about the game. </div> </div> </div> Or I can voice my criticism towards a game I love but to which I see some major failures that are easily fixable, in order to improve it.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it's you who should go away, since you have nothing to add other than blind adherence to whatever set of rules the game has, no matter how flawed they might be, and you also have nothing to add but being passively - aggressive confrontational and showing veiled insults. By the way, isn't that forbidden by the forum's rules?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, a lot of us think HDYDT utterly failed at it's job. You're not saying anything useful with this. </div> </div> </div> Again, passively - aggressively insulting me. Will you stop by your own or do I have to ask for moderation intervention?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides the fact that I did, it's impossible to do what you're asking, because of two important factors. First, the Spheres are inherently abstract and have levels of interpretation. There are always going to be effects that one person feels should be an X level one, that someone else feels is going to be a Y level effect. Even the far better delineated version of the system in Awakening 2e only lessens the impact of this, it can't remove it completely. Second for most intentions there are multiple potential effects that could accomplish the task. Life 3 is the most obvious way to heal someone, but you can create a Wonder with a Life 2 effect they activate (or it activates on its own), high level Entropy can repair instead of destroy, Matter can create medicines and so on, Spirit can call on spirits with healing powers, etc. </div> </div> </div> Some level of abstraction is fine, but there's no need to purposefully create additional confusion for no good reason.<br /> <br /> Also &quot;several ways to do something&quot; is different from total chaos nonsense. In your own examples, half of them are completely irrelevant, one is exactly one of the many problems of the Spheres descriptions. Creating antibiotics with Matter will heal someone... Perhaps... After a few weeks or months... So no, it's absolutely NOT the same as Life 3. Heal someone using Spirits requires dealing with an extra dimensional being, and it's this &quot;ultraterrestrial&quot; that does the healing, NOT YOU. So, irrelevant.<br /> <br /> Using Entropy 4 is fine because IT MAKES SENSE. It's widely different from many other poorly thought examples, because this one actually makes sense and is well constructed <br /> <br /> As for Life 2 vs Life 3, this is one PERFECT example of the nonsensical writing of the Spheres. A life pattern is a life pattern, no matter if the self or another. It is absolutely nonsensical to have effects on self be a level less than on others. Affecting oneself is EASIER, but NOT <b>less complex</b>.<br /> <br /> And this is already expressed in the rules by the required number of successes; you don't need any additional successes to affect yourself, but you need to &quot;spend&quot; 1 success to affect any other pattern other than yourself (and you can keep spending 1 success for each extra target).<br /> <br /> Thus, Life 3 should be used to heal any mammal (probably any vertebrates), with all successes being translated fully to healing for yourself, but with 1 success being subtracted from the total if healing another. And that's it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The book literally says Forces 3 combined with Mind allows you to convert thoughts into energy. Don't lecture about strict adherence to what the Spheres do what Forces 3 explicitly does this when combined with other Spheres according to its description. . </div> </div> </div> And &quot;da Holy Book&quot; also says a ton of other nonsensical things. Some of which I've already described above. So what?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Electrical information is expressed as electrical patterns, yes. </div> </div> </div> Only under a strict Technocratic paradigm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or you just copy them since that's within the Sphere levels being used. </div> </div> </div> Question: if I use Mind 2 and Matter 4 to turn someone's thinking about a table into a physical table, do the thought about the table remains stored?<br /> <br /> Physical transformations are permanent. Once you turn something into something else, particularly for Matter or Forces, the change is permanent and irreversible. So, once you turn thoughts into energy, they cease to be thoughts and only become energy. They are thoughts no longer.<br /> <br /> You cannot store thoughts into energy any more than you could store silver into a lightning by using Matter 2 / Forces 3.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why can't you store them? </div> </div> </div> Just look above <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I change water into air, I can breathe the air. I could put the air in a balloon and float the balloon. It doesn't cease to exist as it's new form.<br /> <br /> Do I need Prime to put air turned into water into a glass? </div> </div> </div>Straw man fallacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Digital information isn't magic. You don't need to &quot;imprint it.&quot; You simply capture the information with Forces.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Neither of these is true the way you're stating them. </div> </div> </div>Nowhere under Forces is stated that it is a Sphere related to information. So no, you don't just simply &quot;capture the information&quot; with Forces.<br /> <br /> And while Digital information isn't magic (but... Isn't it thou? Debatable. You seem to have a poor grasp about Consensus and the true &quot;irrealism&quot; of the setting), I think you have a poor grasping about what Prime actually do.<br /> <br /> Prime is not just a &quot;Meta-Magic&quot; or &quot;Mana Sphere&quot;. Prime is a Sphere that fundamentally rearranges the structures of Patterns.<br /> <br /> Forces by itself has NO capacity to hold information.<br /> <br /> Prime on the other hand, does, because Prime fundamentally rearranges the Patterns of anything. Mental constructs can't exist in a vaccum, thoughts cannot exist on the Ether. Thoughts need either a brain or a soul/spirit. Mental constructs can manifest on living beings or spiritual beings. They don't manifest in objects or energy. But if you combine Prime (and Forces) you could indeed make an energy Pattern hold thoughts (transfered by Mind obviously). So, with Prime and Forces, you could use Mind for transfer memories into an &quot;eternal flame&quot; for example.<br /> <br /> Imprinting memories into objects or energy patterns adding Prime is not much different from creating artefacts. Mind patterns cannot be &quot;fixated&quot; into things without it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Life 5/Forces 3 lets you copy the Human Torch's living fire and flight powers. You don't need any Prime for that. </div> </div> </div> Again, you're just throwing random Spheres without full understand of them, just like many writters do. Why Life 5? What purpose does Life 5 hold in here? If you can already levitate and create and control fire with just Forces 3? Unless you truly want to turn your entire body into fire, you don't need that.<br /> <br /> Also, again, Straw Man fallacy. Life and Forces patterns are material Patterns. Mind Patterns are Ephemeral Patterns. Your comparison is just a Straw Man that doesn't make any sense.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T07:57:27-07:00","id":1523823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523771#post1523771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, this got out of hand a little. Anyway, here's another question. Supposing that a Technomage, whether traditional or a technocrat, wanted to download information from a person's memory and transfer it to a machine, like a smartphone for example, what spheres would be needed? I believe that as there is transference, so Correspondence 2 is necessary and Mind 2 (at least) since it involves memories, but would anything else be necessary? Life or Matter, perhaps.<br /> <br /> Also, let's avoid going into the subject of how much human memory fits in a machine's memory, that's not the focus.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so, you would like to take the memories out of someone's head and convert them in to something else which can be carried around with you. There are a number of different ways one could achieve this.<br /> <br /> First, you will need Mind sphere, this is a given. And in order to access memories you would need at least Mind 3 to view them, and Mind 4 to manipulate them. Whether you need to view or to manipulate will depend on what it is you are going to do else with them.<br /> Going with the idea of converting the person's memories in to something you can carry around with you, this would essentially be a form of transmutation, this would require manipulation levels of Mind, so Mind 4 for memories, Mind 3 for surface thoughts and Mind 2 for feelings, sensations, and vague impressions. What you transmute them in to to remove them from the person's mind would depend on which sphere you were using, transmute them into a solid object with Matter, a living thing with Life, or a form of energy with Forces, there are of course caveats for each.<br /> <br /> For Matter, the level of matter will dictate the form said memory will take. Matter 2 lets you transmute materials, so said object would be something quite simple like a stone, glass orb, a paper disc, very few features to speak of. Matter 3 lets you shape matter objects, and so you could make something like a key, a cup, a candlestick, a fine mist you can bottle or a water you can drink. Said objects would, if interacted with appropriately, may give you glimpses of the memory within, using the key on the correct door can give you an insight into what the memory contains, liquids held in a cup could reflect aspects of said memory, candles burning in the candlestick may let you see aspects of the memory play out in the shadows it casts. Matter 4 lets you create more complex objects, this would be how you could create a flashdrive out of it, and just as with the above examples, using it appropriately may let you experience the memories. Just double clicking on the file may sudden give you than sensation of living through it.<br /> <br /> Life would be very similar to Matter, but the steps would be Life 3 to transmute it in to a simple living pattern, such as a plant, seed, or an insect, or graft it on to a part of your own body like making this memory a third eye for your head. Life 4 to transmute it into a part of someone else's body or to transmute the memory in to some kind of animal, and Life 5 to transform it into a specific living creature of higher order, like a human. The exact level of Life required may be a bit debatable for some paradigms, but I hope this gives you an idea of the concept at least.<br /> <br /> Forces would provide you that option to transform the memory in to something energy connected. Now, the danger here is such a thing would not last very long without having something in place to contain it. Transforming the memory in to light will let you see the memory, turning it into electricity might let you feel the memory as it arcs around the room and hits whomever, turning in to fire would have it burn in a manner befiting whatever the memory depicted, etc. It might even be that some memories are so unlike a particular form of energy that to transform it into an opposing energy might indeed alter, change, or otherwise cause some form of reaction. A memory that was steeped in darkness, for example, might fade quickly when transformed in to light. A memory which is about a harsh rage could cause a great inferno when turned to fire, but might be altered to one of gentle loathing if transformed into cold energy. Stuff for the ST to play around with based on paradigm and resonance of course. And all these examples would only require the addition of Forces 3<br /> So, to transform your target's memories into electricity which can be stored on your flashdrive, Mind 4 Forces 3 would have you covered for that, however, if the flashdrive isn't suitably large enough to store it, or if the memories are so strong and violent they could cause damage, well, they might not stay in that flashdrive for very long, and even worse they might burst out at the first sign of failure of the flashdrive. Mundane objects like that were not really designed for holding electrified memories after all. Again, thing for the ST to play with.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to do any of this from a distance you would need to appropriate level of correspondence (corr = to higher sphere).~<br /> <br /> However, if your goal is to simply view these memories on a device, you do not need to transform memories at all. Instead, this could all be done as a form of scrying using your smart device as an instrument to enable scrying. To do this, all you need is the Viewing level of Mind (for memories this would be simply Mind 3) and the appropriate level of correspondence (in this case, corr 3).<br /> The memories aren't being taken away, changed, or stored, they are simply being accessed from a distance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T12:35:41-07:00","id":1523829,"title":"","content":"I think by convention I'll look at it this way. If I want to transfer memories or even a person's consciousness to a machine I would use mind 3 for memory and mind 4 to transfer his entire ego (or copy it) and forces 3 for conversion. If I just wanted to watch or transcribe a memory I do it with mind 3 and correspondence 3. If I wanted to transfer it to an object like a mirror or a book I would need the &quot;primordium&quot; sphere to insert quintessence into the object.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T12:40:44-07:00","id":1523830,"title":"","content":"I know that if you create a healing potion or something, you need life (variable level) matter and prime, I think. But suppose I don't want or can't use life, could I use time instead? Like returning the state of the wound to before it was made? In this case would I also need entropy?I know that if you create a healing potion or something, you need life (variable level) matter and prime, I think. But suppose I don't want or can't use life, could I use time instead? Like returning the state of the wound to before it was made? In this case would I also need entropy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T13:33:25-07:00","id":1523832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523829#post1523829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think by convention I'll look at it this way. If I want to transfer memories or even a person's consciousness to a machine I would use mind 3 for memory and mind 4 to transfer his entire ego (or copy it) and forces 3 for conversion. If I just wanted to watch or transcribe a memory I do it with mind 3 and correspondence 3. If I wanted to transfer it to an object like a mirror or a book I would need the &quot;primordium&quot; sphere to insert quintessence into the object.</div> </div> </div> </div>This does go against how Mind works in the book, where you need Mind 3 to transfer surface thoughts between people via the mental link, meaning to transfer memories is the next rank up.<br /> <br /> This is because Mind treats transferring thoughts to anyone but yourself as the same level as altering thoughts.<br /> <br /> logic wise this is comparable to being able to use Prime 2 to absorb quintessence in to your pattern, but Prime 3 to pass quintessence between objects or people.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 10-08-2023, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T15:19:49-07:00","id":1523837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523805#post1523805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And here's a question: Aren't thoughts already electrical impulses?\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Sorry, got a bit over-focused on just the system.<br /> <br /> Thoughts aren't just electrical impulses. We have, IRL, wonderfully advanced machines for measuring the electrical activity in the human brain, but we keep hitting a wall when it comes to trying to decode thought. It is possible we just need an insanely larger dataset than we currently have and probably a high end AI algorithm to brute force it all, but it's far more likely that the well know chemical mediators of neural activity create too much &quot;noise&quot; in the electrical field to ever capture thoughts that way. Or, in other words, because our brains aren't circuits, the way the biochemistry of brain activity impacts the electrical part of the equation is essential to what constitutes a &quot;thought.&quot; <br /> <br /> As a basic example, if you're feeling cold, you might think of having a warm beverage, or to put on an additional layer of clothing. What you think of doing is impacted by mixture of chemical and electrical signals in your brain. We can follow the electrical impulse of your temperature sensory pathways from your skin to your brain, but once they're in the brain they get filtered through that complex mixture of chemical and electric filters that leads to a specific inclination towards what &quot;kind&quot; of cold you feel and thus what kind of solution you feel would be best to take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523830#post1523830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that if you create a healing potion or something, you need life (variable level) matter and prime,</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need Matter to craft Wonders out of inert materials. The skilled manipulation of your materials via Abilities (even if sometimes things like Esoterica or Hypertech) is considered sufficient for something like a healing potion. While not specified directly, you would only need Matter in a case like enchanting a natural spring to produce water with healing properties. You can think of this as basically the rules' answer to a Ship of Theseus style issue. If the target for a Wonder is going to be made up of the same components a year later as it is now, you don't need extra Spheres beyond Prime and whatever Spheres for the effect itself. If the components would change over time, you need to add a Sphere relative to the target you're making into a Wonder. This is also the justification for why Matter is unique here: other Sphere's deal with phenomena that are in states of change. You need Life to turn a living pattern into a Wonder to address that life grows, changes, and replaces itself over time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But suppose I don't want or can't use life, could I use time instead? Like returning the state of the wound to before it was made? </div> </div> </div>The problem is that you can't target a wound specifically without Life. You would have to rewind the entire target (and you need Entropy to set a conditional point in time like &quot;when I got injured&quot;). For an injury this might not be so bad since you're dealing with relatively short time scales,but there's a lot of problems with using Time because the books want Time magic to not get wildly out of hand. Considering how much the game does not like time travel or going overboard with reversing time and so on, avoiding Life is a really rough choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T21:57:58-07:00","id":1523860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1523420-using-the-spheres?p=1523815#post1523815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or I can voice my criticism towards a game I love but to which I see some major failures that are easily fixable, in order to improve it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m pretty sure you would be welcome to complain as much as you like\u2026 in your own thread devoted to the complaining. Beyond a certain point - by now exceeded, I would say, although the moderators would have the last word on that - the complaints cease to add anything of value to the topic Psicose introduced in this thread, and continuing to fruitlessly pursue them here becomes just plain rude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11151-travisjhall","name":"travisjhall","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T19:43:59-07:00","id":1524082,"title":"","content":"AI is already able to do some rudimentary &quot;mind reading&quot; based on brain scans. I saw one AI reading the mind of a person listening to a Pink Floyd song, and then turning its readings back into music, and although it ain't a perfect translation, it's still impressive and... Scary.<br /> <br /> The Machine-God we are creating will not only be able to disassemble and reassemble matter on a molecular level using nanomachines, not only will it be able to create materials and energy sources we can't even dream about right now, will be billions of times smarter than all of us combined, but it will also be able to read our minds.<br /> <br /> Thoughts, as it seems, really are just electric impulses in the brain. But that only applies for real life, not necessarily for the MtA game which is a Kantian-Gnostic immaterialistic world<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}